---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { testimonials } from '../../data/site.js';

const quote = testimonials[0];
const toc = [
  ['scope', 'Scope'],
  ['aftercare', 'Aftercare'],
  ['nailshade', 'NailShade'],
  ['career', 'Career Path'],
  ['foundations', 'Engineering notes'],
  ['stack', 'Stack'],
];
---
<Base
  title="Case study: Aftercare, NailShade and Career Path | Bagas Aria Sativa"
  description="Three business applications built end to end for a service company: an aftercare platform for ratings and follow-up, a QR booking platform with a customer points program, and an HR information system."
  path="/case-study/rainbrow/"
  current="case"
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow"><Icon name="layers" /> Case study</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Aftercare, booking and HR for a service company</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">Three applications for a beauty service company with several branches, developed in parallel by one developer while the HR Supervisor guided the business processes. This page explains what each one does and the decisions behind it. Company data is not shown.</p>
      <dl class="facts" style="max-width:46rem">
        <div><dt><Icon name="user" size={14} />Role</dt><dd>Full-stack developer, sole builder</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="calendar" size={14} />Period</dt><dd>Jan 2025 to Oct 2025</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="building" size={14} />Company</dt><dd>Rainbrow Sulam Alis</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="check" size={14} />Delivery</dt><dd>Three apps, ahead of schedule</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:1rem">
    <div class="container doc">
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <p>On this page</p>
        {toc.map(([id, label]) => <a href={`#${id}`} data-toc={id}>{label}</a>)}
      </nav>

      <div class="prose">
        <section id="scope">
          <h2><Icon name="compass" /> Scope</h2>
          <p>The company needed three separate tools: one to follow up on what customers say after a visit, one to take bookings and reward loyal customers, and one to manage its people. They were built as independent applications, side by side, from the day I joined until each was finished. I wrote all three; the HR Supervisor directed and supervised the work across all of them, explaining how it really happens and reviewing the results.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="aftercare">
          <h2><Icon name="star" /> Aftercare</h2>
          <p>The largest of the three: the working tool of the aftercare team for collecting and following up on customer ratings, with nine user roles.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Ratings you can trust.</strong> Customers rate through a tokenised link, scores are validated, and duplicate or unverified feedback is flagged so the numbers hold up.</li>
            <li><strong>Low-rating follow-up.</strong> A low score opens a follow-up case with comments, a conclusion, a voucher and proof of what was done, and it can be reopened.</li>
            <li><strong>Google rating tracking.</strong> Proof records and Excel exports for ratings left on Google.</li>
            <li><strong>Reminders.</strong> A daily job finds customers who have not given feedback, and WhatsApp messages are prepared for staff to send, singly or in bulk.</li>
            <li><strong>After the visit.</strong> Retouch and reschedule handling with photo proof, customer invoice entry, and therapist records with discipline and points.</li>
            <li><strong>Inventory chain.</strong> Purchase requests, receiving, warehouse, pack assembly and delivery to branches, with logistics approval and PDF output.</li>
            <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> Dashboards per branch and per therapist.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="nailshade">
          <h2><Icon name="phone2" /> NailShade</h2>
          <p>A booking and loyalty platform for nail studios, used by customers on their phones, by nail artists at the studio, and by customer service and admin.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>QR booking.</strong> Customers book from their own phone, and walk-in customers register through a QR code at the studio.</li>
            <li><strong>Less typing for artists.</strong> The nail artist scans the barcode the customer shows, then marks the visit and updates the treatments, instead of entering data by hand.</li>
            <li><strong>Points program.</strong> Customers with an account earn points from what they spend, once a spend threshold is reached, and move through tiers from Bronze to Platinum. Points can be redeemed for goods, services or discounts.</li>
            <li><strong>Vouchers.</strong> Percentage or fixed discounts with a minimum spend, claimed by the customer and applied at booking.</li>
            <li><strong>Leaderboard and ratings.</strong> Ratings are tied to the nail artist, and the artist leaderboard supports monthly commission.</li>
            <li><strong>Customer service tools.</strong> Booking management, reschedule and cancellation, and rating links sent through WhatsApp.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="career">
          <h2><Icon name="users" /> Rainbrow Career Path</h2>
          <p>A human resource information system for the whole company. Its core is training and recruitment, alongside the usual HR modules.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>People.</strong> Employee management with admin, manager and staff roles.</li>
            <li><strong>Attendance.</strong> GPS-based attendance with the location validated on the server, so the check cannot be bypassed by editing the page.</li>
            <li><strong>Leave, payroll and performance.</strong> The standard cycle for each, in one place.</li>
            <li><strong>Training and recruitment.</strong> Training scheduling with completion tracking, and recruitment.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="foundations">
          <h2><Icon name="shield" /> Engineering notes</h2>
          <p>The aftercare application went through a security pass: CSRF protection on every form and AJAX call, rating links based on tokens instead of guessable numbers, password hashes upgraded to bcrypt on login, and consistent login checks. The same discipline carried into the much larger <a class="link-arrow" href="/case-study/erp/"><span>ERP case study</span></a>.</p>
          <figure class="quote" style="margin-top:2rem;flex:initial">
            <blockquote style="font-size:var(--step-1)">{quote.quote}</blockquote>
            <figcaption><strong>{quote.name}</strong><span>{quote.role}, {quote.org}</span></figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section id="stack">
          <h2><Icon name="code" /> Stack</h2>
          <p>Aftercare and NailShade: CodeIgniter 3, PHP and MySQL, with Bootstrap for the admin screens and Tailwind CSS for the mobile screens of NailShade, plus jQuery, Chart.js, QR code scanning and WhatsApp click-to-chat links. Career Path: PHP and MySQL. Hosted on Hostinger.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/#contact">Talk about a similar project <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
